{"text": "When we say that water is clean. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> We do not just mean. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> That it looks like a glass of water. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Water quality is about following a certain set of criteria. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Or benchmarks. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> These guidelines inform us. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Exactly how much physical, chemical, or biological stuff. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Can be in the water. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> These rules ensure. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> The water is safe for anything we want to do with it. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Whether that is drinking it at home. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Watering crops on a farm. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Or running it through a huge industrial boiler. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> We cannot utilize the same one size fits all rule for everyone. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Because we use water. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> For so many diverse things. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> For instance. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> The water that cools down a huge power plant generator. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Does not need to be as clean. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> As the water you drink from the kitchen tap. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> This is why groups set different safety limits for the water. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Dependent on how it will be utilized.", "alignment": {"characters": ["W", "h", "e", "n", " ", "w", "e", " ", "s", "a", "y", " ", "t", "h", "a", "t", " ", "w", "a", "t", "e", "r", " ", "i", "s", " ", "c", "l", "e", "a", "n", ".", " ", "<", "b", "r", "e", "a", "k", " ", "t", "i", "m", "e", "=", "\"", "0", ".", "8", "s", "\"", " ", "/", ">", " ", "W", "e", " ", "d", "o", " ", "n", "o", "t", " ", "j", "u", "s", "t", " ", "m", "e", "a", "n", ".", " ", "<", "b", "r", "e", "a", "k", " ", "t", "i", "m", "e", "=", "\"", "0", ".", "8", "s", "\"", " ", "/", ">", " ", "T", "h", "a", "t", " ", "i", "t", " ", "l", "o", "o", "k", "s", " ", "l", "i", "k", "e", " ", "a", " ", "g", "l", "a", "s", "s", " ", "o", "f",